<title>USA: EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS - WSC - 18-AUG.</title>
<headline>EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS - WSC - 18-AUG.</headline>
<text>
<p>Typhoon Winnie is expected to make landfall on the east coast of China, just south of Ningbo, in about 6 hours. Top winds will be 75-80 mph at the time of landfall but will rapidly drop off as the storm moves northwestward into inland areas, then turns north northwest and dissipates within 24 hours. Heavy rainfall will be the main problem from this storm, as it is expected to cause flash flooding and mudslides southwest of Shanghai during the next 24 to 36 hours.</p>
</text>
